cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dreamd in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dreamd: auditable memory for AI coding agents"
abstract: >-
  dreamd is a local-first, single-binary memory layer for AI coding agents.
  Claude Code, Cursor, Cline and other MCP clients share one store of plain
  JSONL and Markdown. Every lesson cites the events it came from, a
  provenance ledger records which event fed which lesson and index entry,
  and a bad memory can be traced and removed with a receipt.
authors:
  - given-names: Phillip Austin
    family-names: Green
    affiliation: Botzr Research Labs
repository-code: "https://github.com/botzrDev/dreamd"
url: "https://dreamd.dev"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.4.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - AI agents
  - coding agents
  - model context protocol
  - MCP
  - provenance
  - local-first
  - Rust
